--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Signing key
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

.env/development_key.pem is an RSA-3072 private key. MCUboot image signing
uses it for every build from this repository (src/sysbuild.conf:12,
src/sysbuild/mcuboot.conf:28). It is committed and public on purpose, for
development only: a signature made with it proves nothing about who produced
an image, and BrainChip's released firmware is not signed with it. The file's
own header says so, and "Application Security" in src/README.md is the
reference. It is the only key material tracked in this repository. The
production key never appears here in any form.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Fetched by the build, not redistributed
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

None of the following is in this repository. The toolchain image built from
docker/Dockerfile, and the host setup in docs/setup.md, fetch them, and each
keeps its own terms.

nRF Connect SDK v3.1.1
    Installed by `nrfutil sdk-manager install v3.1.1` together with its
    toolchain bundle (docker/Dockerfile:52-66 and 87). The SDK's west manifest
    brings its components at matching revisions, among them:

        sdk-nrf v3.1.1           LicenseRef-Nordic-5-Clause (text above)
        sdk-zephyr ncs-v3.1.1    Apache License 2.0 (Zephyr RTOS)
        sdk-mcuboot ncs-v3.1.1   Apache License 2.0 (the bootloader this
                                 firmware builds, src/sysbuild.conf:3)
        sdk-nrfxlib v3.1.1       LicenseRef-Nordic-5-Clause

    and the other modules the manifest lists, each under the licence in its
    own tree. Clause 4 of the Nordic licence restricts that software to use
    with a Nordic Semiconductor ASA integrated circuit; this firmware is built
    for the nRF5340 (docker/Dockerfile:83).

nRF Util
    The nrfutil executable is downloaded from files.nordicsemi.com without a
    version pin (docker/Dockerfile:37-42, scripts/install_nrfutil.sh:9), and
    its sdk-manager 1.9.1 and device 2.15.4 commands are installed through it
    (docker/Dockerfile:59-62). Nordic Semiconductor's own terms apply.

SEGGER J-Link Software V8.88
    docker/tools/README.md asks you to download the .deb from SEGGER and accept
    SEGGER's terms yourself; the image installs it from that local file
    (docker/Dockerfile:144-148), which .gitignore:19 keeps out of the
    repository.

Python packages
    scripts/requirements.txt pins the packages the image installs
    (docker/Dockerfile:133-135), and Zephyr's own scripts/requirements.txt is
    installed from the SDK (docker/Dockerfile:128). The BrainChip MetaTF
    packages akida, cnn2snn, quantizeml and akida_models come from PyPI under
    the BrainChip Software End User License Agreement,
    https://doc.brainchipinc.com/license.html. west, bleak, imgtool,
    python-dotenv, PyYAML and pyserial come from PyPI under their own
    licences. src/utils/requirements.txt lists bleak for the host-side BLE
    scripts. The lint job installs clang-format 23.1.0 from PyPI
    (.github/workflows/ci-gates-lint.yml:114-122).

Operating system packages
    The image is built from ubuntu:22.04 with packages from Ubuntu's archives,
    and Python 3.12 from the deadsnakes PPA (docker/Dockerfile:1-27 and
    100-109).

Models
    No model is in this repository. src/utils/fetch_model.py downloads the
    .fbz named by a local, git-ignored config (.env/<app>/<model>.yaml; see
    "Model build config" in src/README.md), and src/utils/kws.py and
    src/utils/mnist.py use pretrained models from the akida_models package.

Continuous integration
    The workflows under .github/workflows use actions/checkout,
    docker/login-action, docker/build-push-action and
    softprops/action-gh-release from GitHub, and publish the toolchain image to
    ghcr.io/brainchip-inc/akidatag-ncs.
